{
	title: 'Touch tab navigation leaves the keyboard closed',
	spec: 'On touch devices (pointer: coarse), the web composer does not automatically focus when mounted, when switching or creating session tabs, or when a session question or picker stops owning focus. Reading and navigating must not summon the on-screen keyboard. Tapping the message textarea still starts editing normally; explicit send/completion editing actions and desktop automatic focus behavior remain unchanged. A browser regression exercises coarse-pointer tab creation and switching with different form states and confirms the composer stays unfocused until deliberately focused.',
